From: TripleU <182648541+TripleU613@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:57:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] J714s image: trust the new developer signer
 547AF6CC...BC5DF9F6

The private half of the developer signer 0DA040FF...B6D116B1 (installer/patches
0007) was lost on 2026-11-24 with the work PC's build directory, so release 10's
inputs could not be signed. The owner approved a new developer signer:
547AF6CCD493E92950561EE94C6BC7CCBC5DF9F6 (ed25519, sign and certify, no
subkeys, "omarchy-m5 J714s developer image inputs (not a production
release)"). The profile's candidate-trust now names it as primary and signing
fingerprint, with its public key (sha256 9ab5d873...); the stage 1
qualification test follows. Nothing else in the policy changes. Images from
release 10 on verify their package set against this key only.

image-builder/test/all on the build host: every suite passes except
test_edge_dispatch_filter's test_the_template_is_the_one_build_mac_image_reads,
which fails the same way on release 9's tree (3469845) and is unrelated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
